\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Oft I in my heart have said:
\par Who shall ascend on high,
\par Mount to Christ, my glorious Head,
\par To bring Him from the sky?
\par Borne on contemplation's wing,
\par Surely I shall find Him there,
\par Where the angels praise their King,
\par And gain the morning star.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Oft I in my heart have said:
\par Who to the deep shall stoop,
\par Sink with Christ among the dead,
\par From thence to bring you up?
\par Could I but my heart prepare
\par By unfeigned humility,
\par Christ would quickly enter there,
\par And ever dwell with  me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. But the righteousness of faith
\par Hath taught me better things:
\par Inward  turn Thine eyes, it saith,
\par While Christ to me it brings;
\par Christ is ready to impart
\par Life to all for life who sigh;
\par In Thy mouth and in Thy heart
\par The word is ever nigh.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

